# tinyBird configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a real key.

# --- Asset storage (0xstash media API) --------------------------------------
# Without a key the emulator still runs from local files; the vault list is
# simply switched off.
#
# Reads are public: the browser fetches asset bytes straight from the CDN. Only
# the server sees this key, and only to list the vault and upload save states.
TINYBIRD_MEDIA_KEY=
TINYBIRD_MEDIA_VAULT=default
# Download project for save states. Your key must be authorised for it.
TINYBIRD_MEDIA_PROJECT=tinybird
# Owner for private saves. One install is one owner; a multi-user deployment
# must set this from an authenticated session, never from the browser.
TINYBIRD_MEDIA_OWNER=local
TINYBIRD_MEDIA_URL=https://media.0xstash.dev

# --- Accounts (0xstash auth API) --------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without a project secret the sign-in panel stays hidden and every
# save belongs to TINYBIRD_MEDIA_OWNER above, which is how a server you run for
# yourself works. With it, saves belong to whoever is signed in.
#
# The browser never sees this or any token: it gets a first-party session
# cookie and this server does the talking. See crates/tinybird-web/src/auth.rs.
TINYBIRD_AUTH_PROJECT_SECRET=
# TINYBIRD_AUTH_URL=https://auth.0xstash.dev
# TINYBIRD_AUTH_PROJECT=tinybird

# --- Contact form (0xstash contact API) -------------------------------------
# Optional. Without a form key the "get in touch" panel on the home page stays
# hidden, because a form that cannot send is worse than no form.
#
# The browser never sees this key: the page posts to /api/contact and this
# server relays it. See crates/tinybird-web/src/contact.rs.
#
# With TINYBIRD_AUTH_PROJECT_SECRET set, sending requires signing in (which the
# home page offers) and the reply address comes from the session. Without it
# there is nobody to sign in as, so the form asks for an address too.
#
# The same key backs /support/tickets, where a signed-in sender reads what they
# sent and replies to it. That needs both: this key names the project, and the
# session's access token names whose tickets they are.
TINYBIRD_CONTACT_KEY=
# The service authorises a form key against the origins registered for its
# project, and a request from this server carries no origin of its own. Set
# this to one your key is registered for if the service refuses without it.
# TINYBIRD_CONTACT_ORIGIN=https://tinybird.example
# TINYBIRD_CONTACT_URL=https://contact.0xstash.dev

# --- Hosting ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Serve ROMs from the local folder. Leave this alone when running the server for
# yourself; set it to "off" for anything reachable from the internet, because
# /local/{path} would otherwise hand your cartridge dumps to whoever finds it.
# TINYBIRD_LOCAL_ROMS=off

# --- Web server -------------------------------------------------------------
# TINYBIRD_WEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# TINYBIRD_WEB_PORT=8877
# TINYBIRD_WEB_SNAPSHOT=stream-data/current-game.json
# TINYBIRD_WEB_SPRITES=stream-data/pokemon-sprites
# TINYBIRD_WEB_WASM=target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/tinybird_wasm.wasm

# The stream overlay is switched off by default: it reads the desktop app's
# export rather than the emulator in the page, and is being reworked. Set to 1
# to serve /overlay/* and show the deck toggle again.
# TINYBIRD_WEB_OVERLAY=1
